# Archive fixtures are byte-exact captures: tests assert on their exact bytes
# (see fixtures/README.md), so Git must neither rewrite them nor mistake a
# producer's own bytes for a whitespace defect.

# Never apply end-of-line conversion. `fixtures/mhtml/` deliberately holds a
# mix: the real Chrome captures are CRLF (RFC 2557/2045 line terminators) while
# `minimal.mhtml` is hand-written LF. A contributor with `core.autocrlf=true`
# would otherwise have both mangled on checkout, breaking byte-exactness for
# whichever kind their platform disagrees with.
fixtures/** -text

# Enable `cr-at-eol` for MHTML fixtures only: a CR immediately before the LF is
# part of the line terminator, not trailing whitespace, so `git diff --check`
# and `git apply` stop reporting every line of a real Chrome capture. This adds
# to Git's default whitespace checks rather than replacing them — a genuine
# trailing space or tab in these files is still reported, as are all whitespace
# errors everywhere else in the repository.
fixtures/mhtml/*.mhtml whitespace=cr-at-eol
